From 3c64d95fc3ee8c3c837a871515539c2e878437c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:16:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(build): publish both Gson variants from one source tree

Build the standard Gson and ViaVersion Gson artifacts from master so model
fixes no longer require a separately maintained vv-json branch. Generate
the ViaVersion main and test sources by replacing the Gson package name.
Compile and run the same regression suite against each actual dependency,
and publish matching generated sources for the ViaVersion artifact.

Carry the geometry and rendering changes already merged into vv-json in
PRs #2 through #6 into the shared standard-Gson source. Retain invisible
and locator-only geometry, optional fields, authored face rotations,
lighting, UV animation, legacy controller declarations, visibility,
parent setup and repeated material assignments. Keep the master map API
as a deprecated compatibility view; ordered assignments retain repeats.
https://github.com/oryxel1/CubeConverter/pull/2
https://github.com/oryxel1/CubeConverter/pull/3
https://github.com/oryxel1/CubeConverter/pull/4
https://github.com/oryxel1/CubeConverter/pull/5
https://github.com/oryxel1/CubeConverter/pull/6

Publish separate Maven modules because the public Gson types and their
runtime dependencies differ. Expose Gson and JOML as API dependencies,
keep Lombok at compile time, and exclude bundled dependency copies. Both
artifacts target Java 17. JitPack and CI build, test and publish both.
Consumers select the named cubeconverter or vv-json artifact; the JitPack
repository aggregate can otherwise put duplicate classes on the classpath.
